      "artist": "Stephen Hogan from Chicago, United States",
      "description": "In 1934 Melvin Purvis was tipped off by madam Anna Sage that public enemy #1 John Dillinger would be attending a movie on the hot night of July 22.  Around 10:30 PM Dillinger came out of the Biograph Theater with Sage and another woman and headed south.  Melvin Purvis saw Dillinger and signalled his G-men who were waiting for him.  Dillinger spotted Purvis and made a run into an alley but was gunned down.  Four bullets entered his body and he died within three minutes.\n\nLocated at 2433 N. Lincoln Avenue.",
